kernelbase: implement FlsGetValue2, the newer FLS lookup UCRT/VCRuntime
probe for and call unconditionally when found.

Missing on upstream Wine (11.0 and later) and on CrossOver's own build too
(checked directly), not just Kalimotxo's — a real Wine gap, not something
specific to this project. A modern native DLL that links a recent UCRT
calls FlsGetValue2() from a hot path expecting it to leave the calling
thread's last-error code untouched, unlike FlsGetValue(). When the symbol
is missing Wine does not fail the GetProcAddress lookup gracefully: it
crashes with an unrelated-looking Wine stack overflow instead. Seen on
Project Diablo 2's Game.exe (PD2_EXT.dll, its own modern native addition
to the original 2000 Blizzard engine) right as it starts, well before any
graphics init — every install of it, not something D3D/graphics-related.

Same shape as FlsGetValue(), routing straight to RtlFlsGetValue() (which
never touches last-error) instead of through set_ntstatus() (which does).

--- a/dlls/kernelbase/thread.c	2026-09-27 23:20:07
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/thread.c	2026-09-27 23:20:07
@@ -1308,6 +1308,26 @@
 
     if (!set_ntstatus( RtlFlsGetValue( index, &data ))) return NULL;
     SetLastError( ERROR_SUCCESS );
+    return data;
+}
+
+
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           FlsGetValue2   (kernelbase.@)
+ *
+ * Newer Windows-internal variant of FlsGetValue(), missing from Wine (and
+ * from real Windows on older builds too): newer UCRT/VCRuntime builds probe
+ * for it via GetProcAddress and call it from a hot path that must not
+ * disturb the calling thread's last-error code, unlike FlsGetValue(). Its
+ * absence used to crash such games and apps with a Wine stack overflow
+ * instead of the graceful fallback a missing GetProcAddress result should
+ * get (e.g. Project Diablo 2's Game.exe via a modern PD2_EXT.dll).
+ */
+PVOID WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH FlsGetValue2( DWORD index )
+{
+    void *data;
+
+    if (!NT_SUCCESS( RtlFlsGetValue( index, &data ))) return NULL;
     return data;
 }
 
